",content:"<p>- What are exchange flows? Exchange flows in cryptocurrencies refer to the movement of digital assets in or out of centralized exchange wallets, reflecting capital transfers between an exchange and other market participants.</p> why are exchange flows important? Monitoring cryptocurrency flows into centralized exchanges can empower investors and traders with valuable insights into market sentiment, identify trading activity resulting from material events, and supply and demand dynamics. This proactive approach helps them make more informed decisions, adapt their strategies, and manage risks more effectively in cryptocurrency markets."},{subject:"Understanding exchange flows",content:"<img alt='Bitcoin: Inter-exchange Flow Pulse (IFP)' src='https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/655db8e0175e0e53b93d2045/chart-image.jpg' /><br/> <a target='_blank' rel='noopener' href='https://cryptoquant.com/analytics/query/644af4f986317b3f85ce9bc6?v=644af66abbe24f02e5e3fe4a'>Bitcoin: Inter-exchange Flow Pulse (IFP)<i class='ic-newopen'></i></a><br/> <ul><li>The IFP focuses on measuring Bitcoin flows between different exchanges, especially flows between spot exchanges (Coinbase in this case) and all derivative exchanges.</li><li>When Bitcoin's Inter-exchange Flow Pulse trends down, it signals that Bitcoin is flowing from derivatives to spot exchanges, which typically occurs during bear markets.</li><li>Conversely, a rising Inter-exchange Flow Pulse indicates that Bitcoin is flowing from spot to derivatives exchanges, which has historically coincided with bull markets.</li></ul>"}],previewImageUrls:["https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/655db8e0175e0e53b93d2045/01.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/655db8e0175e0e53b93d2045/02.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/655db8e0175e0e53b93d2045/03.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/655db8e0175e0e53b93d2045/04.png"],blockedEmailDomains:["kakao.com","comcast.net","yahoo.com","hanmail.net","hotmail.com","daum.net","naver.com","gmail.com","aol.com"],utm:{medium:"prospects",campaign:"applied-research",content:"Exchange-Flows-as-a-Market-Risk-Management-Tool"},createdAt:"2023-12-01T00:00:00.000Z"},"6538dcf3ec21aa51c8da47c9":{id:"6538dcf3ec21aa51c8da47c9",title:"From Hashrate to Treasury Management: Leveraging Miner Data for Market Insights",subTitle:"Hacking the Bitcoin Miners' Strategy",keySummaries:["Project the supply and demand from the miners.","Gauge miners' profitability in real-time.","Signal $BTC price and market cycle direction."],keyTakeaways:["Monitoring Bitcoin transfers in and out of miner's wallets helps time the market, indicating profit-taking at price peaks and loss realization at price bottoms.","Bitcoin miners' data, such as block rewards and mining difficulty, provides investors with insights into miners' overall profitability, helping to determine if Bitcoin's price action is sustainable.","Historically speaking, extreme transfers out of miner's wallets coincided with important inflection points for Bitcoin price and the market cycle."],descriptions:[{subject:"Who is a Bitcoin miner and why is Bitcoin miner's data important?",content:"<p>A Bitcoin miner verifies and adds transactions to the blockchain while securing the network and earning rewards in the form of newly created bitcoins and transaction fees. </p> <span class='highlight'>Miners' data is crucial for various stakeholders.</span>  Traders rely on it to spot short-term price trends, as shifts in miner flows and profitability indicate changes in market sentiment. Strategic investors use miner analysis to assess the current state of the mining industry, while miners themselves utilize it for treasury management and gaining a competitive edge. Lastly, market analysts integrate it into their cryptocurrency research, which enhances their forecasts."},{subject:"Understanding the sustainability of miner's revenue",content:"<img alt='Bitcoin: Miner Profit/Loss Sustainability' src='https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6538dcf3ec21aa51c8da47c9/chart-image.jpg' /><br/> <a target='_blank' rel='noopener' href='https://cryptoquant.com/analytics/dashboard/63064a8d77d099261f5ddfb8'>Bitcoin: Miner Profit/Loss Sustainability<i class='ic-newopen'></i></a><br/> <ul><li>Extremely high levels of miners' revenue relative to mining difficulty correspond to price tops in each market cycle and price corrections within market cycles.</li><li>Conversely, extremely low levels of miners' revenue relative to mining difficulty correspond to price bottoms in each market cycle or serve as local price supports within the market cycles.</li><li>Consequently, monitoring the overall profitability of Bitcoin miners can help investors manage their risk and exposure to Bitcoin.</li></ul>"}],previewImageUrls:["https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6538dcf3ec21aa51c8da47c9/01.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6538dcf3ec21aa51c8da47c9/02.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6538dcf3ec21aa51c8da47c9/03.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6538dcf3ec21aa51c8da47c9/04.png"],blockedEmailDomains:["kakao.com","comcast.net","yahoo.com","hanmail.net","hotmail.com","daum.net","naver.com","gmail.com","aol.com"],utm:{medium:"prospects",campaign:"applied-research",content:"Leveraging-Miner-Data-for-Market-Insight"},createdAt:"2023-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},"657a9a1a83ad92251f8f638f":{id:"657a9a1a83ad92251f8f638f",title:"Risk Management: Managing and Monitoring Centralized Exchange Risks With CryptoQuant",subTitle:"Data sets to identify the next FTX",keySummaries:["Determine exchange's solvency by its reserves","Measure the bank run possibility by withdrawals","Address trading activity anomaly with on-chain"],keyTakeaways:["Investors, traders, and market makers can leverage CryptoQuant's data to manage and monitor the risks associated with having their funds on centralized exchanges.","We introduce the Exchange Risk Monitor Model, which defines the type of data and the specific metrics that can be tracked in order to evaluate centralized exchange risk in real-time.","We demonstrate how market participants could have anticipated rising risks on the FTX exchange months before its collapse using CryptoQuant's proprietary data and the Exchange Risk Monitor Model."],descriptions:[{subject:"What are exchange reserves and why is exchange reserves data important?",content:"<p>Exchange reserves refer to the total amount of cryptocurrencies or digital assets held by a centralized exchange in its own centralized wallets or accounts. </p><span class='highlight'>Exchange reserves serve two vital roles: covering customer withdrawals and maintaining trading liquidity.</span> The amount of reserves held indicates an exchange's financial health and its ability to handle sudden withdrawal spikes. Monitoring reserve data is essential for investors to detect suspicious practices, such as exchanges artificially inflating reported reserves to create a false impression of higher liquidity."},{subject:"Foreseeing the collapse of the FTX exchange.",content:"<img alt='Bitcoin: Exchange Trading-Volume-To-Reserve Ratio (TVR Ratio)' src='https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/657a9a1a83ad92251f8f638f/chart-image.jpg' /><br/> <span class='img-desc'>Bitcoin: Exchange Trading-Volume-To-Reserve Ratio (TVR Ratio)</span><br/> <ul><li>It is important to monitor the trading volume of an exchange relative to its reserves to determine the amount of leverage on the exchange and assess possible wash trading activity.</li><li>The chart shows how FTX exchange trading volume for Bitcoin relative to its Bitcoin reserves continued to increase while all other exchange’s were declining.</li><li>This indicated wash trading or increasing leverage (risk) on the exchange prior to its collapse.</li></ul>"}],previewImageUrls:["https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/657a9a1a83ad92251f8f638f/01.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/657a9a1a83ad92251f8f638f/02.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/657a9a1a83ad92251f8f638f/03.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/657a9a1a83ad92251f8f638f/04.png"],blockedEmailDomains:["kakao.com","comcast.net","yahoo.com","hanmail.net","hotmail.com","daum.net","naver.com","gmail.com","aol.com"],utm:{medium:"prospects",campaign:"applied-research",content:"Managing-and-Monitoring-Centralized-Exchange-Risks"},createdAt:"2023-11-13T00:00:00.000Z"},"6639ffb84385336955c34eea":{id:"6639ffb84385336955c34eea",title:"Enhancing On-chain Analysis: Cohort-based Data and Metrics by CryptoQuant",subTitle:"Unlock Crypto Trends via Cohorts",keySummaries:["Project the key support price of early investors","Monitor smart money’s quiet accumulation","Analyze whale behavior for investment edge"],keyTakeaways:["Cohort data analysis offers a significant enhancement over traditional on-chain data analysis by allowing addresses to be grouped by multiple characteristics simultaneously.","By grouping addresses into cohorts based on different and simultaneous criteria, analysts can study and compare the behavior and characteristics of different segments of a blockchain user base or network participants. ","We analyze a specific cohort in the Bitcoin network: the permanent holder. We show that understanding this cohort allow us to estimate the growth in the demand for Bitcoin as an investment asset, as this cohort is composed of entities that accumulate Bitcoin overtime and never sell. "],descriptions:[{subject:"What is a cohort and why is cohort data important?",content:"<p><b class='text-text-primary'>What is a cohort?</b>  In the context of on-chain data analysis, a cohort refers to a group of addresses that share similar characteristics or exhibit similar behaviors within a blockchain network.</p> <b class='text-text-primary'>Why is cohort data important? </b>Cohort data analysis offers a significant enhancement over traditional on-chain data analysis by allowing addresses to be grouped by multiple characteristics simultaneously, rather than just one characteristic."},{subject:"Assessing Bitcoin Demand Growth With Cohort Data",content:"<img alt='Bitcoin Balance of Permanent Holders' src='https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6639ffb84385336955c34eea/chart-image.jpg' /><br/> <a target='_blank' rel='noopener' href='6639ffb84385336955c34eea'>Bitcoin Balance of Permanent Holders<i class='ic-newopen'></i></a><br/> <ul><li>The 30-day growth in the balances of Bitcoin permanent holders captures the demand for Bitcoin from companies and institutions. </li><li>In a first phase the demand for Bitcoin fluctuated between 5K and 50K Bitcoin in a 30-day period as companies started to buy.</li><li>In the current phase the demand for Bitcoin has spiked to as high as 200K Bitcoin in a 30-day period, mostly driven by purchases from ETFs in the USA.</li></ul>"}],previewImageUrls:["https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6639ffb84385336955c34eea/01.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6639ffb84385336955c34eea/02.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6639ffb84385336955c34eea/03.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6639ffb84385336955c34eea/04.png"],blockedEmailDomains:["kakao.com","comcast.net","yahoo.com","hanmail.net","hotmail.com","daum.net","naver.com","gmail.com","aol.com"],utm:{medium:"prospects",campaign:"applied-research",content:"Enhancing-On-chain-Analysis-Cohort-based-Data-and-Metrics"},createdAt:"2024-05-01T00:00:00.000Z"},"6639ffec4eb5eb3ddd54d90b":{id:"6639ffec4eb5eb3ddd54d90b",title:"Leveraging Blockchain Data for Equity Investing - Bitcoin Mining Companies",subTitle:"Leveraging Blockchain Data for Equity Investing - Bitcoin Mining Companies",keySummaries:["Monitor miner strategy, revenues & holding","Manage Risks: Instant Data on Minier’s sell-off","Get ahead of the market with insider data"],keyTakeaways:["In the context of Bitcoin mining companies, blockchain data can be used to monitor a company’s revenue, Bitcoin holdings, and Bitcoin selling in real-time.","Understanding these data is advantageous to those investing or analyzing Bitcoin mining related equities, as on-chain data is real-time as opposed to data from public filings which come with a significant delay.","This approach empowers investors with the agility to react swiftly to mining companies' production trends, treasury management and company valuation, enhancing their ability to make informed and timely investment decisions and stay ahead of the mining company's financial reports and production updates"],descriptions:[{subject:"Why is real time On-chain data useful for equity analysis of publicly traded Bitcoin mining companies?",content:"<p><b class='text-text-primary'>Why is real time On-chain data useful? </b>  By incorporating on-chain data that tracks the real-time Bitcoin production and holdings of mining companies, investors gain an immediate and granular insight into the operational aspects of these firms.</p> <b class='text-text-primary'>what is the advantage of having access to real time On-chain data for equity investment?</b> Utilizing on-chain data to monitor publicly listed Bitcoin mining companies offers a significant advantage over relying solely on quarterly reports, as it provides real-time insights into their operational performance and financial health."},{subject:"Anticipating Production Trends of Bitcoin Mining Companies ",content:"<img alt='Bitcoin: Miner Profit/Loss Sustainability' src='https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6639ffec4eb5eb3ddd54d90b/chart-image.jpg' /><br/> <a target='_blank' rel='noopener' href='https://cryptoquant.com/community/dashboard/6566303dbd919d7cba94c50d'>Marathon Digital Daily Bitcoin Production<i class='ic-newopen'></i></a><br/> <ul><li>The chart hows the daily Bitcoin production for Marathon Digital. We can observe how daily production declined from a high of 115 Bitcoin on December 14, 2023 to a low of 6.6 Bitcoin in January 26, 2024. </li><li>This sharp decline in daily Bitcoin production was mostly the result of the company experiencing some equipment failures and weather-related disruptions during January 2024.</li><li>However, this was only known to traditional finance analysts on February 4, 2024 when the company announced its monthly production update. By noticing the Bitcoin production decline, an analyst could have anticipated Marathon's operation disruptions and act accordingly.</li></ul>"}],previewImageUrls:["https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6639ffec4eb5eb3ddd54d90b/01.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6639ffec4eb5eb3ddd54d90b/02.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6639ffec4eb5eb3ddd54d90b/03.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6639ffec4eb5eb3ddd54d90b/04.png"],blockedEmailDomains:["kakao.com","comcast.net","yahoo.com","hanmail.net","hotmail.com","daum.net","naver.com","gmail.com","aol.com"],utm:{medium:"prospects",campaign:"applied-research",content:"Leveraging-Blockchain-Data-for-Equity-Investing"},createdAt:"2024-05-03T00:00:00.000Z"},"6639fff4f919457d1576444d":{id:"6639fff4f919457d1576444d",title:"Ethena - USDe’s Tail Risks Analysis and Key Metrics to Monitor",subTitle:"Enhancing On-chain Analysis Cohort-based Data and Metrics by CryptoQuant",keySummaries:["Understand unique USDe funding risks","Track Ethena's reserve growth needs","Ensure stable USDe peg with metrics"],keyTakeaways:["USDe is a recently launched stablecoin that has grown to a market capitalization of over $2 billion in a shorter time after launch than any other major stablecoin. USDe was launched by Ethena Labs.","Ethena maintain its peg and generates yield by opening short positions in futures market. However, this exposes USDe to unique risks not present in other stablecoins. One of these risks is the funding risk.","We analyze USDe’s funding risks in extremely adverse scenarios and conclude that, in order for this risk to be minimized, the Ethena reserve fund should grow in par with the market capitalization of USDe, and the keep rate (the amount of yield that goes into the reserve fund) should remain above 20% in order for the reserve fund to grow fast enough and be well capitalized.","Investors with exposure to USDe need to monitor and make sure that Ethena's reserve fund and keep rate are appropriate to the growing market capitalization of USDe."],descriptions:[{subject:"What is Ethena's reserve fund? and why is Ethena's reserve fund important?",content:"<p><b class='text-text-primary'>What is Ethena's reserve fund?</b> The reserve fund acts as an additional margin of safety behind USDe to provide a source of capital to pay for periods of negative funding, as well as a bidder of last resort for USDe in open markets.</p> <b class='text-text-primary'>Why is Ethena's reserve fund important?</b> It allows Ethena to pay for keeping its short positions open in period of negative funding rates. If the reserve fund runs out, short positions could be liquidated and USDe's peg lost."},{subject:"What are the risks that Ethena faces for maintaining the USDe peg?",content:"<img alt='Ethena Cumulative Funding Payments: ETH Negative Funding Rate Scenario After the Merge and the Collapse of FTX' src='https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6639fff4f919457d1576444d/chart-image.jpg' /><br/> <a href='none'>Ethena Cumulative Funding Payments: <br/>ETH Negative Funding Rate Scenario After the Merge and the Collapse of FTX.<i class='ic-newopen'></i></a><br/> <ul><li>The current reserve fund ($32.7 million) would be enough to cover funding payments as long as USDe market cap is not larger than $3 billion (current market cap is $2.4 Billion). </li><li>To safely manage the extraordinary event of large negative funding rates at larger market capitalizations of $4 billion, $5 billion, $7.5 billion or $10 billion, the reserve fund would need to increase to about $40 million, $50 million, $80 million and $100 million, respectively.</li></ul>"}],previewImageUrls:["https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6639fff4f919457d1576444d/01.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6639fff4f919457d1576444d/02.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6639fff4f919457d1576444d/03.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6639fff4f919457d1576444d/04.png"],blockedEmailDomains:["kakao.com","comcast.net","yahoo.com","hanmail.net","hotmail.com","daum.net","naver.com","gmail.com","aol.com"],utm:{medium:"prospects",campaign:"applied-research",content:"Enhancing-On-chain-Analysis-Cohort-based-Data-and-Metrics"},createdAt:"2024-05-06T00:00:00.000Z"},"669a0f30a2747a751c8fa4aa":{id:"669a0f30a2747a751c8fa4aa",title:"The TRON Stablecoin Edge: Activity and Retail Payments with USDT",subTitle:"The TRON Stablecoin Edge: Activity and Retail Payments with USDT",keySummaries:["TRON’s High TPS and Scalability Explained","USDT Dominance and Activity on TRON Network","Retail Users Drive TRON’s Transaction Volume"],keyTakeaways:["The activity on the TRON network is heavily dominated by the transfer of Tether’s stablecoin, USDT. As of June 2024, USDT represented more than 99% of the total transfers made by the top 10 smart contracts on TRON. This overwhelming dominance highlights the critical role that USDT plays within the TRON ecosystem, making it on of the key drivers of network activity.","Additionally, USDT on TRON represents a substantial portion of the overall USDT supply, with more than 53% share as of 2024. TRON's low transaction fees and high transaction speeds have made it a preferred platform for USDT transactions, especially among retail users for smaller, everyday transactions. ","The median transaction value of USDT on TRON is consistently lower than on Ethereum, indicating that TRON is widely used by retail users for smaller transactions. This broad user base drives high transaction volumes and liquidity, enhancing TRON’s role as a cost-effective solution for remittances, micropayments, and peer-to-peer transfers."],descriptions:[{subject:"Why is stablecoin data important?",content:"<p>Stablecoins play a crucial role in the cryptocurrency ecosystem by providing a stable store of value and facilitating seamless transactions. </p> Capturing a significant market share of the stablecoin total market capitalization is crucial for a blockchain like TRON for several strategic and practical reasons."},{subject:"Most holders of USDT on TRON could be classified as “retail” or small holders. ",content:"<img alt='Most holders of USDT on TRON could be classified as “retail” or small holders' src='https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/669a0f30a2747a751c8fa4aa/chart-image.jpg' /><br/><a href='https://cryptoquant.com/community/dashboard/669849f78990c054fac8cf6c'>USDT on TRON: Number of Holders by Balance Cohort<i class='ic-newopen'></i></a><br/><ul><li>These holders with a total USDT balance less than US$1,000 amount to 52.6 million.</li><li>The amount of small USDT holders has grown constantly, even during the 2022 crypto bear market.</li><li>Small USDT holders make almost one third of total USDT transactions on TRON. </li></ul>"}],previewImageUrls:["https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/669a0f30a2747a751c8fa4aa/01.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/669a0f30a2747a751c8fa4aa/02.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/669a0f30a2747a751c8fa4aa/03.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/669a0f30a2747a751c8fa4aa/04.png"],blockedEmailDomains:["kakao.com","comcast.net","yahoo.com","hanmail.net","hotmail.com","daum.net","naver.com","gmail.com","aol.com"],utm:{medium:"prospects",campaign:"applied-research",content:"TRON-Stablecoin-Edge-Activity-and-Retail-Payments-with-USDT"},createdAt:"2024-07-18T00:00:00.000Z"},"66a33cdc97da046e35b3a94f":{id:"66a33cdc97da046e35b3a94f",title:"TON, The People's Network - A Blockchain Built on a Massive Community Foundation",subTitle:"TON: The People’s Blockchain",keySummaries:["How TON leverages Telegram’s 900M user base","Explore TON’s impressive 50x network activity growth","Understand TON’s potential for future scalability"],keyTakeaways:["TON possesses various characteristics that give the network the potential to achieve substancial growth: 1. The seamless integration of TON with Telegram’s 900 million monthly active users, and 2. the network architecture that would allow TON to scale and onboard this massive amount of users.","The integration of TON’s ecosystem into Telegram gives TON’s network a direct exposure to Telegram’s huge community, which has grown to about 900 million users. Indeed, TON’s user base could have immense growth potential as it stands at around 25 million active users so far in 2024, representing only about 3% of Telegram’s userbase.","We found that TON has experienced accelerating network activity growth so far in 2024, with key network metrics like active addresses (users), transfers and total fees showing 4x-50x growth since the start of the year."],descriptions:[{subject:"Analyzing TON blockchain data, including metrics like the number of active addresses, transfers, and fees, is essential to assess the growth of the network and the adoption rate. ",content:"<p>Monitoring the number of active addresses provides insight into the network's adoption rate. A growing number of active addresses indicates a thriving ecosystem with more users engaging in transactions. </p>Tracking transfers on the TON blockchain helps to gauge the level of activity and utility within the network. A growing amount of transfers suggests that the network is being used for its intended purpose."},{subject:"TON-Telegram integration",content:"<img alt='TON Total Annual Active Addresses and Telegram Users' src='https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/66a33cdc97da046e35b3a94f/chart-image.jpg' /><br/><a href='https://cryptoquant.com/community/dashboard/66a2c8757f2e5503acdb2af9'>TON Total Annual Active Addresses and Telegram Users<i class='ic-newopen'></i></a><br/><ul><li>The integration of TON’s ecosystem into Telegram gives TON’s network a direct exposure to Telegram’s huge community, which has grown to about 900 million users.</li><li>Indeed, as shown in the chart above, TON’s user base could have immense growth potential as it stands at around 25 million active users so far in 2024, representing only about 3% of Telegram’s userbase.</li><li>In this respect, it can be argued that TON is building a blockchain on top of an already existing and huge community, whereas most projects start building a community on top of a blockchain. The later can be much harder than the former. </li></ul>"}],previewImageUrls:["https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/66a33cdc97da046e35b3a94f/01.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/66a33cdc97da046e35b3a94f/02.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/66a33cdc97da046e35b3a94f/03.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/66a33cdc97da046e35b3a94f/04.png"],blockedEmailDomains:["kakao.com","comcast.net","yahoo.com","hanmail.net","hotmail.com","daum.net","naver.com","gmail.com","aol.com"],utm:{medium:"prospects",campaign:"applied-research",content:"TRON-Stablecoin-Edge-Activity-and-Retail-Payments-with-USDT"},createdAt:"2024-07-24T00:00:00.000Z"},"66de3a5681794d4e45d87789":{id:"66de3a5681794d4e45d87789",title:"USDT on TON: Enhancing Liquidity and Value Transfer on The Network",subTitle:"USDT Growth and Impact on TON Network",keySummaries:["Explore TON’s stablecoin liquidity growth.","Learn how USDT powers P2P value transfers.","Understand USDT’s role in TON’s DeFi ecosystem."],keyTakeaways:["TON is attracting the stablecoin liquidity necessary to power network expansion. The total supply of USDT, the largest stablecoin, on TON has grown to $729 million in the four months after the TON Foundation announced the integration of USDT into Telegram (April 18th). If USDT on TON was a standalone stablecoin it would be the seventh largest by market capitalization.","USDT on TON is suited for fast adoption of P2P value transfer. The median transfer amount, fluctuating around modest values of $15-$100, indicates frequent smaller transactions typical of everyday retail activities. Simultaneously, the consistently low median transfer fee on TON, remaining at four cents, makes these transactions economically viable for users.","USDT is also making its way into TON in the form of high usage in Decentralized Exchanges (DEXs). The DeFi ecosystem of USDT on TON is predominantly shaped by interactions from Decentralized Exchanges (DEXs)."],descriptions:[{subject:"Why are stablecoins  important for Blockchains? ",content:"<p>Stablecoins play a crucial role in the cryptocurrency ecosystem by providing a stable store of value and facilitating seamless transactions. Among the various stablecoins, Tether’s USDT is the largest by total market capitalization and of the most widely used.</p><br/> Capturing a significant market share of the stablecoin total market capitalization is crucial for a blockchain like TRON for several strategic and practical reasons."},{subject:"USDT Entity Activity and Use",content:"<img alt='USDT on TON: Entities With More USDT Activity' src='https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/66de3a5681794d4e45d87789/chart-image.jpg' /><br/><a href='https://cryptoquant.com/community/dashboard/66982a660a078b098fee2903?e=66983070b31f1e652088caed'>USDT on TON: Entities With More USDT Activity<i class='ic-newopen'></i></a><br/><ul><li>The ecosystem of USDT on TON is predominantly shaped by interactions from three primary types of entities: Decentralized Exchanges (DEXs), Centralized Exchanges (CEXs), and various wallet services. </li><li>The top entities facilitating these interactions include the DEXs Ston.Fi, Dedust, and StormTrade, several centralized exchange addresses, and wallet services like XRocket, CryptoBot, Wallet Bot, and CWallet.</li><li>The transaction count data suggests there is higher weight of user adoption from wallet applications that focus on P2P USDT transfers. This implies that P2P transfer apps have potential for growth.</li></ul>"}],previewImageUrls:["https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/66de3a5681794d4e45d87789/01.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/66de3a5681794d4e45d87789/02.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/66de3a5681794d4e45d87789/03.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/66de3a5681794d4e45d87789/04.png"],blockedEmailDomains:["kakao.com","comcast.net","yahoo.com","hanmail.net","hotmail.com","daum.net","naver.com","gmail.com","aol.com"],utm:{medium:"prospects",campaign:"applied-research",content:"USDT-on-TON-Enhancing-Liquidity-and-Value-Transfer-on-The-Network"},createdAt:"2024-09-07T00:00:00.000Z"},"66ece03adf4fe46be75ce4bf":{id:"66ece03adf4fe46be75ce4bf",title:"XRPL's Decentralized Exchange 2.0: Bringing Together The Best of Orderbook and AMM Protocols",subTitle:"New Opportunities on XRPL DEX 2.0",keySummaries:["Explore billions of transactions & future growth.","Experience enhanced trading with XLS-30.","Find out how XRPL reduces common trading risks."],keyTakeaways:["XRPL is introducing a new Decentralized Exchange protocol based on Automated Market Makers (AMM): XLS-30. By integrating the AMM design, XRPL can now bring together the advantages of both LOB and AMM designs, while minimizing the two protocols’ disadvantages by complementing each other.","XLS-30’s innovative features and integration with the existing LOB can provide better price execution and improved liquidity, while minimizing some of the most common pitfalls of AMM’s, such as MEV and front-running.","In the last decade, XRPL has processed more than 3.0 billion transactions, with 441 million transactions in 2023. Most of these transactions are of the type that place offers on XRPL’s native Central Limit Order Book (CLOB) Decentralized Exchange (DEX)."],descriptions:[{subject:"Why is the AMM DEX implementation on XRPL important?",content:"<p>By integrating the CLOB with the AMM DEX, traders gain access to both CLOB and AMM liquidity pools, which enhances liquidity depth. This integration allows traders to execute trades at more competitive prices by tapping into the liquidity available in both markets simultaneously. Additionally, the integration can facilitate arbitrage opportunities between the CLOB and AMM DEX, further improving pricing efficiency and market dynamics. </p>"},{subject:"XRPL CLOB Decentralized Exchange",content:"<img alt='XRPL: Most Used DEX Trading Pairs for XRP (# of OfferCreate Transactions in 2023)' src='https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/66ece03adf4fe46be75ce4bf/chart-image.jpg' /><br/><a href='https://cryptoquant.com/community/dashboard/66aa6a6e00442146d87661c8?e=66aa6ed292025e70b10cf8a5'>XRPL: Most Used DEX Trading Pairs for XRP (# of OfferCreate Transactions in 2023)<i class='ic-newopen'></i></a><br/><ul><li>The XRPL CLOB DEX largely uses XRP for fiat currency exchange. Specifically, the XRP/CNY (Chinese Yuan) trading pair represented 42% of the total offers created in 2023. </li><li>The offers created to trade XRP for US dollars represented almost 10%. Additionally, almost 8% of offers were to exchange XRP for stablecoins USDC and USDT.</li><li>Major non-XRP trading pairs, include Bitcoin/US dollar, Euro and Bitcoin with FLR (Flare) and the fiat currency pairs involving the US dollar and Euro.</li></ul>"}],previewImageUrls:["https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/66ece03adf4fe46be75ce4bf/01.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/66ece03adf4fe46be75ce4bf/02.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/66ece03adf4fe46be75ce4bf/03.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/66ece03adf4fe46be75ce4bf/04.png"],blockedEmailDomains:["kakao.com","comcast.net","yahoo.com","hanmail.net","hotmail.com","daum.net","naver.com","gmail.com","aol.com"],utm:{medium:"prospects",campaign:"applied-research",content:"USDT-on-TON-Enhancing-Liquidity-and-Value-Transfer-on-The-Network"},createdAt:"2024-09-07T00:00:00.000Z"},"6735b165516fc00c0b2420c1":{id:"6735b165516fc00c0b2420c1",title:"From Telegram to Trading: The Emergence of DEX Activity on TON",subTitle:"TON Is Transforming DEX Trading",keySummaries:["Discover TON’s $3.5B DEX trading surge","Understand why DEXs matter for blockchain","Learn how new pools can fuel TON’s growth"],keyTakeaways:["Decentralized Exchange (DEX) activity emerged on TON in 2024. DEX activity has seen $3.5 billion in total trading volume and $13 million as daily average. Additionally, The total US dollar value (TVL or total value locked) in the DEXs we analyze has grown from basically zero in April 2024 to about $300 million at the time of writing.","The integration of the USDT stablecoin has been key for the DEX growth activity on TON. DEX TVL on TON has seen growth in 2024 mostly after the stablecoin USDT was integrated into the network on April 2024.","STON.fi and DeDust are dominating the DEX landscape on TON. These two DEX applications have concentrated DEX trading activity on TON, with total trading volume on DeDust totaling $1.7 Billion so far in 2024,\xa0 and $1.8 Billion for STON.fi. Daily active users and transaction have also been trending up. DEXs on TON have the advantage of integrating their platform directly into the Telegram app."],descriptions:[{subject:"Why are {DEXs} important for blockchains?",content:"<p>The growth of a DEX ecosystem is vital for the success and sustainability of a blockchain network. DEXs bring liquidity and transaction activity to a blockchain, which are essential for increasing the value and utility of the native token and other assets built on the network. A thriving DEX ecosystem also attracts developers, traders, and liquidity providers, creating network effects that fuel further growth.</p>"},{subject:"KEY DEX METRICS AND ACTIVITY ON TON",content:"<img alt='DeDust: Total Value Locked by Pool ($)' src='https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6735b165516fc00c0b2420c1/chart-image.jpg' /><br/><a href='https://cryptoquant.com/community/dashboard/6717b577de32434fd99cad12'>DeDust: Total Value Locked by Pool ($)<i class='ic-newopen'></i></a><br/><ul><li>DEX TVL on TON has seen growth in 2024 mostly after the stablecoin USDT was integrated into the network on April 2024. </li><li>Indeed, total TVL on DeDust is concentrated on pools that use USDT to trade for TONCoin (TON), Tonstakers (tsTON) and staked TON (stTON).</li><li>The USDT/TON pool has a TVL of $68 million, $44 million are in USDT/tsTON and $15 in USDT/stTON.</li></ul>"}],previewImageUrls:["https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6735b165516fc00c0b2420c1/01.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6735b165516fc00c0b2420c1/02.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6735b165516fc00c0b2420c1/03.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6735b165516fc00c0b2420c1/04.png"],blockedEmailDomains:["kakao.com","comcast.net","yahoo.com","hanmail.net","hotmail.com","daum.net","naver.com","gmail.com","aol.com"],utm:{medium:"prospects",campaign:"applied-research",content:"From-Telegram-to-Trading-The-Emergence-of-DEX-Activity-on-TON"},createdAt:"2024-11-14T00:00:00.000Z"},"6785e7879e66406395c30c08":{id:"6785e7879e66406395c30c08",title:"2024 TRON Network Review: From USDT Powerhouse to DeFi Hub",subTitle:"TRON’s Growth Beyond Stablecoins",keySummaries:["Discover the $236M fee growth sustaining TRON","Explore TRON’s 94,000 meme tokens and impact","Learn why SunSwap leads TRON’s DeFi revolution"],keyTakeaways:["In 2024, while USDT activity continued to dominate the TRON network, there was a notable surge in decentralized trading and meme coin creation. The use of TRX, TRON's native currency, and its wrapped version, WTRX, increased significantly, driven by DeFi interactions on platforms like SunSwap. The launch of the SunPump application further amplified speculative activity by making meme coin creation accessible, leading to a wave of new tokens and heightened transaction volumes. This diversification of on-chain activity highlights TRON's expanding ecosystem beyond stablecoin transfers, reinforcing its role as a hub for both utility-driven and community-led blockchain activity.","USDT continues to be a major force behind network activity. The supply of USDT on TRON grew from $48 billion to $62 billion in 2024, while the value transferred increased from $362 billion in December 2023 to $576 billion in December 2024, with monthly transfers rising from 55 million to 62 million. USDT is by far the most transferred token on TRON, accounting for as much as 99% of token transferred. It is worth noting that TRON, in collaboration with Tether and TRM Labs, fights cryptocurrency-related financial crime and reach the milestone by frozen more than $100 million in criminal assets globally.","However, 2024 marked a significant inflection point of DeFi activity on the TRON network. SunSwap, the leading DEX on TRON, saw a sharp rise in usage, with 4 million monthly transactions recorded in August 2024—97% of these involving WTRX. From August to year-end, total swap transactions reached 8.3 million, demonstrating significant DeFi growth. Over 80% of all swaps on SunSwap in 2024 involved WTRX, with WTRX swap volumes growing from 4.2 billion to 20 billion units or $4.1 billion by December 2024."],descriptions:[{subject:"What is TRON's {SunPump}?",content:"<ul class='mb-4'><li>{SunPump}, introduced in 2024, is a decentralized platform designed to simplify the deployment of meme coins on the TRON blockchain. The application provides users with an intuitive interface to launch customizable tokens with minimal technical knowledge, fueling a wave of new meme coins such as Sundog and SUNCAT.</li><li>Daily total created tokens on SunPump grew rapidly after its launch, totaling 7.5k on August 20. As of December 2024, 94k tokens had been launched on SunPump.</li><li>This surge in meme coin creation and trading contributed to increased transaction volumes, particularly in the second half of the year, as users also flocked to SunSwap to trade these tokens. The ease of creating meme coins through SunPump amplified speculative activity and user engagement, showcasing the growing demand for creative and community-driven token projects.</li></ul>"},{subject:"DEX Impulse: Sunswap",content:"<img alt='TRON SunSwap: Total Transactions' src='https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6785e7879e66406395c30c08/chart-image.jpg' /><br/><a href='https://cryptoquant.com/community/dashboard/677301a3a315a278ef5978ad?e=6779c115a315a278ef634b72'>TRON SunSwap: Total Transactions<i class='ic-newopen'></i></a><br/><ul><li>In 2024, the surge in WTRX transactions was largely driven by its use in the SunSwap DEX, which reached a record-high 4 million monthly transactions in August, with 97% involving WTRX.   </li><li>From August to December 2024, SunSwap recorded 8.3 million total swap transactions, with WTRX participating in over 80% of them. This marks a significant leap from 2023, when monthly swaps never exceeded 200,000.</li><li>his explosive growth underscores the increasing role of decentralized trading in TRON's ecosystem, positioning WTRX as a critical liquidity asset and demonstrating the network’s ability to support large-scale DeFi activity</li></ul>"}],previewImageUrls:["https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6785e7879e66406395c30c08/01.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6785e7879e66406395c30c08/02.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6785e7879e66406395c30c08/03.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6785e7879e66406395c30c08/04.png"],blockedEmailDomains:["kakao.com","comcast.net","yahoo.com","hanmail.net","hotmail.com","daum.net","naver.com","gmail.com","aol.com"],utm:{medium:"prospects",campaign:"applied-research",content:"2024-TRON-Network-Review"},createdAt:"2025-01-14T00:00:00.000Z"},"678715e66054db6fcb524948":{id:"678715e66054db6fcb524948",title:"2024 Crypto Survey:\xa0Exchange Use and Investor Behavior",subTitle:"Insights on Today’s Crypto Investors",keySummaries:["Explore trader demographics and behaviors","Find data-driven insights on trading habits","Discover top exchange preferences"],keyTakeaways:["Binance dominates globally as the preferred exchange, except in North America, where Coinbase leads. A total of 53% of respondents use Binance as their primary exchange, 48% hold most of their assets on Binance, and half report their highest profits were obtained on Binance","The Investment focus remains on Bitcoin, Ethereum, and Layer 2 solutions, with emerging interest in AI and blockchain integration.","Bybit, Binance, OKX, and Bitget attract a larger share of full-time traders (more than 30%). Meanwhile, Coinbase, Crypto.com, and Kraken cater primarily to part-time traders (more than 80%), reflecting their focus on casual investors. The difference could also be explained by the distinct preferences of traders in the exchange’s core regions."],descriptions:[{subject:"What are the exchange {earn} products?",content:"<ul class='mb-4'><li>What is {earn} products? : Earn products\xa0are financial services offered by cryptocurrency exchanges that allow users to earn passive income on their crypto holdings. These products typically include options like\xa0staking,\xa0savings accounts,\xa0yield farming, and\xa0liquidity provision. Users can lock or lend their assets in exchange for rewards, such as interest, new tokens, or a share of platform fees. These products appeal to long-term holders seeking to grow their investments without active trading. </li><li>what are the implications of {earn} products responses for exchanges? : Exchanges have still room to grow their earn products as only 28% of respondents use them regularly</li></ul>"},{subject:"Description of the highlighted chart",content:"<img alt='Description of the highlighted chart' src='https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/678715e66054db6fcb524948/chart-image.jpg' /><br/><br/><ul><li>In 2024, the surge in WTRX transactions was largely driven by its use in the SunSwap DEX, which reached a record-high 4 million monthly transactions in August, with 97% involving WTRX.   </li><li>From August to December 2024, SunSwap recorded 8.3 million total swap transactions, with WTRX participating in over 80% of them. This marks a significant leap from 2023, when monthly swaps never exceeded 200,000.</li><li>his explosive growth underscores the increasing role of decentralized trading in TRON's ecosystem, positioning WTRX as a critical liquidity asset and demonstrating the network’s ability to support large-scale DeFi activity</li></ul>"}],previewImageUrls:["https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/678715e66054db6fcb524948/01.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/678715e66054db6fcb524948/02.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/678715e66054db6fcb524948/03.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/678715e66054db6fcb524948/04.png"],blockedEmailDomains:["kakao.com","comcast.net","yahoo.com","hanmail.net","hotmail.com","daum.net","naver.com","gmail.com","aol.com"],utm:{medium:"prospects",campaign:"applied-research",content:"Exchange-Use-and-Investor-Behavior"},createdAt:"2025-01-14T00:00:00.000Z"},"68230dd80fc5ac762e6cccc7":{id:"68230dd80fc5ac762e6cccc7",title:"Monitoring Bitcoin Miner Revenues: A Framework for Equity Valuation",subTitle:"Find Undervalued Bitcoin Miners",keySummaries:["Identify mispriced public mining companies","Compare miner value using real-time data","Improve investment timing and strategy"],keyTakeaways:["CryptoQuant’s on-chain data platform tracks the daily revenue of Bitcoin mining companies through its proprietary labeling methodology, which pinpoints addresses on the Bitcoin blockchain belonging to specific mining companies. We track the Bitcoin production of public Bitcoin mining companies including: MARA, RIOT, CORZ, HIVE, CLSK, BITF, WULF, CIPHER and IREN (with virtually 100% accuracy.)","By estimating daily mining revenues directly from block rewards, and transaction fees, attributed to known miner addresses, analysts can derive daily (intra-month) revenue metrics that are unavailable through traditional corporate disclosures. When these revenue estimates are annualized and compared to the market capitalization of publicly-traded mining firms, they offer a forward-looking valuation framework similar to a price-to-sales ratio. ","Access to real-time revenue data of Bitcoin mining companies via on-chain analysis provides investors with a powerful tool to assess relative valuations across the sector. By comparing each company's market capitalization to its annualized revenue on a daily basis, investors can identify which firms are potentially overvalued or undervalued. This enables more informed portfolio allocation—favoring companies whose market valuations lag behind their revenue generation while reducing exposure to those trading at excessive premiums. "],descriptions:[{subject:"Why have access to data about the daily revenues of publicly traded Bitcoin mining companies?",content:"<p>Having access to this data opens opportunities for relative value strategies by identifying firms that may be lagging in market recognition despite solid operational performance. Investors could implement several delta-neutral trading strategies to capitalize on valuation disparities between overvalued and undervalued Bitcoin mining companies, particularly using pair trading approaches.  </p>"},{subject:"Description of the highlighted chart",content:"<img alt='IREN: Annualized Revenue and Market Cap' src='https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/68230dd80fc5ac762e6cccc7/chart-image.png' /><br/><a href='https://cryptoquant.com/community/dashboard/6786d1de1001ca2735a9a749'>IREN: Annualized Revenue and Market Cap<i class='ic-newopen'></i></a><br/><ul><li>IREN’s market cap increase is not supported by revenues. </li><li>The Market cap increase is supported by higher revenues.</li><li>The decline of IREN’s market cap since March is not justified compared to the company’s higher revenue.</li></ul>"}],previewImageUrls:["https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/68230dd80fc5ac762e6cccc7/01.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/68230dd80fc5ac762e6cccc7/02.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/68230dd80fc5ac762e6cccc7/03.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/68230dd80fc5ac762e6cccc7/04.png"],blockedEmailDomains:["kakao.com","comcast.net","yahoo.com","hanmail.net","hotmail.com","daum.net","naver.com","gmail.com","aol.com"],utm:{medium:"prospects",campaign:"applied-research",content:"Monitoring-Bitcoin-Miner-Revenues-A-Framework-for-Equity-Valuation"},createdAt:"2025-05-13T00:00:00.000Z"},"6879da9bed3b8d78b4e87ef6":{id:"6879da9bed3b8d78b4e87ef6",title:"1H 2025 TRON Network Review: USDT Dominance and DeFi Momentum\xa0",subTitle:"TRON’s Stablecoin Takeover",keySummaries:["TRON flips Ethereum in USDT supply","Network usage hits multi-year highs","DeFi growth reshapes TRON’s ecosystem"],keyTakeaways:["TRON Network Activity Hits Multi-Year Highs. TRON processed 273 million transactions in May 2025—its second-highest monthly total ever—while active addresses reached 28.7 million in June, the highest since mid-2023.","TRON Overtakes Ethereum in USDT liquidity. The total USDT supply on TRON reached a new all-time high of $80.8 billion, surpassing Ethereum’s $73.8 billion, and rising 35% year-to-date.","SunSwap DEX Sees Sustained Growth in DeFi Activity. Monthly swap volumes for WTRX have remained above $3 billion in 2025, peaking at $3.8 billion in May, while monthly transactions average 516K—up from 2024 levels. WTRX's dominance in swap activity declined from 98% in August 2024 to 70% in June 2025, indicating growing DeFi activity around stablecoins and other tokens."],descriptions:[{subject:"Why is important to follow USDT activity on TRON?",content:"The surge in USDT supply on TRON signals the network’s growing dominance as the primary settlement layer for stablecoin transactions. This increase in liquidity enhances TRON's role as a core infrastructure for crypto payments and remittances."},{subject:"USDT: TRON OVERTAKES ETHEREUM IN USDT LIQUIDITY AND ACTIVITY",content:"<img alt='USDT: Total Supply on TRON and Ethereum' src='https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6879da9bed3b8d78b4e87ef6/chart-image.png' /><br/><a href='https://cryptoquant.com/community/dashboard/686404e2d839184a616f0efe?e=68641b7ee8e47a34c96bd73f'>USDT: Total Supply on TRON and Ethereum<i class='ic-newopen'></i></a><br/><ul><li>TRON has overtaken Ethereum in terms of total USDT supply, and the activity of USDT on TRON continues to be much higher than on Ethereum. The total supply of USDT on TRON reached a new all-time high of $80.8 billion, compared to $73.8 billion on Ethereum. USDT’s supply on TRON is up by $21 billion or 35% so far in 2025.</li></ul>"}],previewImageUrls:["https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6879da9bed3b8d78b4e87ef6/01.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6879da9bed3b8d78b4e87ef6/02.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6879da9bed3b8d78b4e87ef6/03.png","https://img.cryptoquant.com/applied-research/6879da9bed3b8d78b4e87ef6/04.png"],blockedEmailDomains:["kakao.com","comcast.net","yahoo.com","hanmail.net","hotmail.com","daum.net","naver.com","gmail.com","aol.com"],utm:{medium:"prospects",campaign:"applied-research",content:"1H-2025-TRON-Network-Review-USDT-Dominance-and-DeFi-Momentum\xa0"},createdAt:"2025-07-18T00:00:00.000Z"}},rI={getPreview:e=>rO[e],getList:()=>["6879da9bed3b8d78b4e87ef6","68230dd80fc5ac762e6cccc7","678715e66054db6fcb524948","6785e7879e66406395c30c08","6735b165516fc00c0b2420c1","66ece03adf4fe46be75ce4bf","66de3a5681794d4e45d87789","66a33cdc97da046e35b3a94f","669a0f30a2747a751c8fa4aa","6639fff4f919457d1576444d","6639ffec4eb5e